// Golden lockstep replay: a real battle on the shipped default arena, with the world
// checksum recorded every `checkpoint_interval` ticks.
//
// Every target (Linux, Windows, macOS ARM64, wasm32-wasip1) replays this script and must
// reproduce `checksums` exactly. A simulation change that alters behaviour updates this
// list in the commit that explains why. See tests/golden_replay_tests.rs.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment WP4 (Q0036): "red_psi" (psi_grey) now
// swings with damage point 0, every 21 ticks, range 0.1, backswing 9 (was 4, 22, 0.3, 6).
// Checkpoints 1 to 4 (ticks 1 to 200) are unchanged; from checkpoint 5 (ticks 201 to 250), the
// first in which the zealot weapon matters, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP6 (Q0038; marine damage point 1, backswing 13) from checkpoint 4 on, and
// for WP7 (Q0039): "blue_infantry" (pulse_bot) now walks at 0.126 per tick (was 0.09), so every
// checkpoint changed from checkpoint 1 (ticks 1 to 50), where the squad starts moving at tick 5.
// Re-recorded for WP8 (Q0039): the Overclock of "blue_infantry" (stimmed at tick 260) lasts 268
// ticks (was 250). Its remaining ticks are world state, so checkpoints 6 and 7 (ticks 251 to 350)
// changed; from checkpoint 8 on the checksums are those of WP7 again: no unit carries the
// Overclock by tick 400 (the stimmed marines have died), so the longer stim changed nothing else.
// Re-recorded for WP15 (Q0045 3b): "overclock_stim" now also unlocks the Overclock of
// shock_golem. The research is completed before tick 1 and each player's unlocked abilities are
// hashed, so every checkpoint changed; no unit's behaviour did (with the units.ron part of the
// change alone, every checkpoint stays as recorded for WP8).
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-battle-flipbook-animation WP2 (checksum schema 9 -> 10): each
// entity's `anim_progress`, a constant zero no system wrote, is no longer encoded, so every
// checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: the render snapshots of all 1000 ticks are byte for byte
// those of schema 9.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment WP9 (D-4): the shield-regeneration delay
// is read from the catalog (still 250), and a new entity's `ticks_since_last_damage` starts at
// u16::MAX ("never damaged") instead of 250. That counter is hashed, so every checkpoint
// changed. No behaviour did: with the spawn value left at 250, every checkpoint stays as
// recorded for flipbook WP2.
// Re-recorded for WP10 (Q0039): every shielded archetype regenerates 0.112 shields per tick (was
// 0.08). Checkpoints 1 to 12 are unchanged; from checkpoint 13 (ticks 601 to 650), when a
// damaged "red_psi" zealot has first gone 250 ticks unhit, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP11 (Q0039): shields start regenerating 179 ticks after the last damage (was
// 250). Checkpoints 1 to 11 are unchanged; from checkpoint 12 (ticks 551 to 600), when that
// zealot now starts regenerating, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group S1 (Q0039): "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) and "red_siege"
// (railgun_crawler) walk at 0.126 per tick (was 0.09, the Normal-time speed). Every checkpoint
// changed from checkpoint 1 (ticks 1 to 50), where "blue_armor" starts moving at tick 5.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group R2 (Q0039): "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) regenerates 0.01531 life
// per tick (was 0, the Roach's 0.2734 per Normal s). Only checkpoints 6 and 8 to 11 (ticks 251
// to 300 and 351 to 550) changed; checkpoints 1 to 5, 7 and 12 to 20 are as before (no
// regenerating beetle's life differs at those checkpoints).
// Re-recorded for WP12 group W1 (Q0039): "red_siege" (railgun_crawler) fires every 19 ticks in
// tank mode (was 26, the Normal-time period). Checkpoints 1 to 3 are unchanged; from checkpoint 4
// (ticks 151 to 200), its first fight after the AttackMove of tick 120, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group W2: "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) fires every 36 ticks (was 28;
// StarCraft II's 2 Normal s). Checkpoints 1 to 3 are unchanged; from checkpoint 4 (ticks 151 to
// 200), the first fight, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group W3: "red_siege" (railgun_crawler) releases its shot 3 ticks into
// the swing (was 4, the Normal-time 0.167 s), in tank and siege mode. Checkpoints 1 to 3 are
// unchanged; from checkpoint 4 (ticks 151 to 200), its first fight, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group W4: "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) releases 3 ticks into its swing (was
// 2; the CWeapon default 0.167 Normal s). Checkpoints 1 to 3 are unchanged; from checkpoint 4
// (ticks 151 to 200), its first fight, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group W5: "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) and "red_siege" (railgun_crawler)
// have the CWeapon default backswing of 9 ticks (was 4). Checkpoints 1 to 3 are unchanged; from
// checkpoint 4 (ticks 151 to 200), their first fights, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group W7: "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) throws its acid at 1.05 per tick (was
// 0.64; the Roach's missile, 18.75 Normal per s). Checkpoints 1 to 4 are unchanged; from
// checkpoint 5 (ticks 201 to 250), every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP17 commit b (D-8 item 4, Q0045 1b): the movement phase no longer snaps a
// turret to its goal; the weapon phase alone turns it, at its rate (21.6 degrees per tick for
// "red_siege", railgun_crawler). Turret angles are hashed, so checkpoints 4 to 6 and 9 (ticks 151
// to 300 and 401 to 450) changed. No behaviour did: with turret angles left out of the checksum,
// every checkpoint of both fixtures equals that of commit a.
// Re-recorded for WP17 commit d (audit §10.3): hull-mounted weapons fire within their StarCraft
// II tolerance (Arc / 2 + ArcSlop: 11.25 degrees for "blue_infantry", "blue_armor" and "red_psi",
// which fired within 15, 15 and 180). A unit whose target is outside it now turns first. Every
// checkpoint from checkpoint 4 (ticks 151 to 200), the first fight, changed.
// Re-recorded for WP17 commit e (audit group W8): the "red_siege" (railgun_crawler) turrets turn
// at 40.32 degrees per tick (was 21.6). Turret angles are hashed, so checkpoint 4 (ticks 151 to
// 200) changed. No behaviour did: the tank's arc is unrestricted, and with turret angles left
// out of the checksum every checkpoint of both fixtures equals that of the turreted-arc commit.
// Re-recorded for WP17 commit f (Q0045 1b): every hull turns at its StarCraft II rate (55.99
// degrees per tick for "blue_infantry", "blue_armor" and "red_psi", 20.16 for "red_siege"; was
// instant). Checkpoint 2 (ticks 51 to 100, the first moves) and every checkpoint from
// checkpoint 4 (ticks 151 to 200) changed.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-turn-before-move WP3 (Q0050): "red_siege" (railgun_crawler)
// turns before it moves. Ordered at tick 120 to AttackMove 104 degrees from its spawn facing, each
// tank turns in place on ticks 121 to 125 (20.16 degrees per tick) and takes its first step on
// tick 126, then walks the path it walked before, five ticks later. Checkpoints 1 and 2 are
// unchanged; from checkpoint 3 (ticks 101 to 150) every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-turn-before-move WP6 (Amendment 1): "red_siege" turns in place
// at its StarCraft II stationary rate, 40.32 degrees per tick (StationaryTurningRate 720, `core`
// UnitData:39). It turns in place on ticks 121 to 123 (was 121 to 125), steps on tick 124 (was
// 126), and walks the same path two ticks earlier. Checkpoints 1 and 2 are unchanged; from
// checkpoint 3 every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP1 (B-1, remediation M-22): a ready weapon
// whose turn this tick brings its target inside the firing arc starts its swing on that tick (it
// started one tick later). Checkpoints 1 to 3 are unchanged; from checkpoint 4 (ticks 151 to 200),
// the first fight, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP4 (B-9, StarCraft II's keep-target rule):
// a unit whose automatic target is out of weapon reach takes the closest candidate of the best
// rank; it no longer keeps chasing its target while a rival is up to 1.0 closer. On tick 213 the
// "red_psi" zealot (entity 24), chasing "blue_infantry" marine 15 2.29 away, out of reach, turns
// to marine 8, 0.006 closer. Checkpoints 1 to 4 are unchanged; from checkpoint 5 (ticks 201 to
// 250) every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP4 (B-11, checksum schema 10 -> 11): each
// entity's `previous_target_position`, where its automatic target last stood, is hashed, so every
// checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: no rule writes the field yet, so it is `None` for every
// entity on every tick, and the encoding only gains its empty tag.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment WP14 Amendment 7 (Q0057, B-12): scan range
// is measured edge to edge, the centre distance minus both collision radii, with every value
// unchanged. On tick 149 "blue_infantry" marine 16 (pulse_bot, scan 9, radius 0.375) acquires
// "red_psi" zealot 22 (psi_grey, radius 0.5) 9.74 between centres, 8.87 between edges; under the
// centre rule it walked on. Checkpoints 1 and 2 are unchanged; from checkpoint 3 (ticks 101 to
// 150) every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP14 Amendment 7 step 2 (Q0057, B-12): every armed unit scans to its
// StarCraft II reference (audit §11.2), "blue_infantry" (pulse_bot) 5.5 (was 9), "blue_armor"
// (rhino_beetle) 5 (was 10), "red_psi" (psi_grey) 5 (was 9), "red_siege" (railgun_crawler) 7.5
// (was 11), edge to edge. On tick 149 marine 16 no longer acquires zealot 22, 8.87 beyond both
// edges; it acquires it on tick 164. Checkpoints 1 and 2 are unchanged; from checkpoint 3 (ticks
// 101 to 150) every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP5 (B-2, checksum schema 11 -> 12): each
// weapon's `strike_interval_ticks` and `followup_max_distance`, each entity's `pending_strikes`
// and each projectile's `strikes` are hashed, so every checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: every
// shipped interval is 0, so every strike still lands on its release tick, and with the four
// fields left out of the encoding (schema 11) both fixtures reproduce as recorded for the scan
// ranges (Q0057).
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP5 (B-2): "red_psi" (psi_grey) lands the
// second blade of each swing 5 ticks after the first, and only within 2.1 of its target (was:
// both on the swing's tick). Checkpoints 1 to 4 are unchanged; from checkpoint 5 (ticks 201 to
// 250), the first in which a zealot swings, every checkpoint changed. golden_replay_orders is
// unchanged: its "red_ledge" zealots swing at nothing before its last checkpoint.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP6 (B-14, checksum schema 12 -> 13): each
// weapon's Armored and Light bonuses are replaced by its bonus against every attribute, encoded
// as eight values, so every checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: with the bonuses encoded as the
// two former fields at schema 12, both fixtures reproduce as recorded for WP5.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP7 (B-15): a strike that breaks the shields
// sends the shield-mitigated damage minus the shields to life (was raw x (1 - shields / mitigated)).
// With shield armour 0, as for every "red_psi" (psi_grey) zealot here, the two are equal in real
// numbers; the old quotient lost about 1e-9 of life to fixed-point rounding at each break. Only
// checkpoints 5, 6 and 8 (ticks 201 to 300 and 351 to 400) changed, while a zealot carried that
// rounding; with the old value substituted wherever the two differ by at most 1e-5 (they never
// differ more, and shield armour is always 0), both fixtures reproduce as recorded for WP6.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP8a (B-16, checksum schema 13 -> 14): a
// splash's three fixed radii become its list of zones (radius and fraction), so the schema byte
// changes every checkpoint. No behaviour did: with the zones encoded at schema 13, both fixtures
// reproduce as recorded for WP7 (no splash weapon is encoded in either replay's state).
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP8b (B-18, checksum schema 14 -> 15): each
// splash also encodes its shape (a circle, or a line's origin, axis and offsets), so the schema
// byte changes every checkpoint. No behaviour did: with the shape encoded at schema 14, both
// fixtures reproduce as recorded for WP8a.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP9 group g10 (B-47): "blue_armor"
// (rhino_beetle) sees 9 (was 10, StarCraft II 5.0.14 `liberty` UnitData:7210). What the squad sees
// is world state from tick 1, so every checkpoint changed. With only the Roach analogue's sight
// restored to 10, both fixtures reproduce as recorded for WP8b.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP9 group g12 (B-47): collision radii as
// StarCraft II 5.0.14 (`CUnit` `Radius`): "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) 0.5 (was 0.5625, the class
// default `core` UnitData:41) and "red_siege" (railgun_crawler) 0.875 (was 0.75, `liberty`
// UnitData:5094). Radii are part of the hashed bodies, so every checkpoint changed. With only
// those two radii restored, both fixtures reproduce as recorded for WP9 group g10.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP9 (B-82, checksum schema 15 -> 16): each
// weapon also encodes its structure strike (none on any weapon here), so the encoding changes
// every checkpoint. No behaviour did: no shipped weapon has a structure strike yet, and the whole
// matrix and battle 33 are bit-identical to WP9 group g12.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP10 (B-29, checksum schema 16 -> 17): each
// weapon's acquisition arc and each unit's engaged target are encoded, so every checkpoint
// changed. No behaviour did: with the two fields left out of the encoding at schema 16, every
// checkpoint stays as recorded for WP9 (the shipped acquisition arcs equal the engaged arcs).
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-05-sc2-deviation-fixes WP10 (B-29): every shipped weapon takes its
// StarCraft II acquisition arc, `Arc` / 2 (0 for every weapon that sets no `Arc`), so a unit faces
// a new target exactly before its first swing. `golden_replay` differs from checkpoint index 3
// (ticks 151 to 200) and `golden_replay_orders` from index 4 (ticks 41 to 50), the first fights;
// with the acquisition arcs set back to the engaged arcs both reproduce as recorded for the schema
// 17 commit.
// Re-recorded for WP10 (B-30, checksum schema 17 -> 18): each weapon's turret idle behaviour and
// rate are encoded, so every checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: with the field left out of the
// encoding at schema 17, every checkpoint stays as recorded for the B-29 data (every shipped
// turret holds).
// Re-recorded for WP11 (B-3, checksum schema 18 -> 19): each weapon's random delay range and each
// unit's carried delay are encoded, so every checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: with the fields
// left out of the encoding at schema 18, every checkpoint stays as recorded for the B-30 data
// (every shipped weapon authors no delay yet).
// Re-recorded for WP11 (B-3 data): every weapon adds StarCraft II's random delay of -0.0625 to
// 0.125 Normal s (-1.1161 to 2.2321 ticks, core WeaponData:35-36) to each attack, drawn from the
// world's seeded generator. The first checkpoint whose ticks hold a release changes (here and in
// the other fixture), and every later one; with the delays at (0.0, 0.0) both fixtures reproduce
// as recorded for schema 19.
// Re-recorded for WP13c (B-43, checksum schema 20 -> 21): each unit's attack dash cooldown is
// encoded, so every checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: with the field left out of the encoding
// at schema 20, every checkpoint stays as recorded for WP13a (no shipped archetype carries a dash).
